🚨 **BLOCKING: CI red on the head — the CRAP ratchet fails on `validateAgentSection` (13.02 > 12.00), added by this PR's rework**

All 4 failed checks in `ci_failures.md` (Quality gate ×2, CRAP + duplication ×2 across the two dispatch runs) trace to ONE root cause. From the CI logs (fetched via `gh run view --job 115577543646` / `115573066565`; `ci_failures_full.log` was absent from the input):

```
13.02   95.0  N/A   13  (top-level).validateAgentSection   lib/src/config/config_service.dart:1290
Max CRAP: 13.02 — FAIL (threshold: 12.00)
```

The "Quality gate" jobs are only the aggregate cascading `R_GUARDS: failure`. The rework's two new `case` branches (`misuseBreaker`, `stuckTool`) grew the function's decision points 6 → 9 (counted on main vs this head); at ~95% coverage the complexity-13 function lands at CRAP 13.02 over the repo's pinned 12.0 ceiling (`crap4dart.yaml:35` — "pushes may only make the codebase BETTER, never worse"). I reproduced the gate locally: `crap4dart check --baseline` passes (duplication baselines clean), the failure is exclusively the coverage-driven CRAP ratchet, so it will stay red until the function is restructured.

Fix — keep the mirror complete but flatten the switch. Two shapes that both fit the file's existing patterns (note `config_service.dart` deliberately cannot import `cli_config.dart` — dart:io — so reuse the mirror-by-value style, not the boot parser's private helpers):

1. Convert the per-key switch into a validator map, exactly like the `_sectionValidators` table this function already sits in:

```dart
const _agentKeyValidators = <String, void Function(Object?)>{
  'contextWindowCap': _validateAgentCapValue,
  'mode': _validateAgentModeValue,
  'misuseBreaker': _validateAgentMisuseBreakerValue,
  'stuckTool': (v) => StuckToolConfig.fromYaml(v),
};

void validateAgentSection(Object? node) {
  if (node is! YamlMap) {
    throw ConfigException('must be a map, got: $node');
  }
  for (final entry in node.entries) {
    final validate = _agentKeyValidators['${entry.key}'];
    if (validate == null) {
      throw ConfigException('unknown "agent" key: ${entry.key}');
    }
    validate(entry.value);
  }
}
```

2. Or extract the existing `contextWindowCap` body (2 `if`s + throw) into `_validateAgentCapValue` — that alone drops the switch function back under the ratchet.

The emitter↔validator parity test you added keeps guarding whichever shape lands. Please re-run the guards leg after the refactor — the ratchet must be green on the head the SM validates.

