The "Quality gate" jobs are only the aggregate cascading `R_GUARDS: failure`. The rework's two new `case` branches (`misuseBreaker`, `stuckTool`) grew the function's decision points 6 → 9 (counted on main vs this head); at ~95% coverage the complexity-13 function lands at CRAP 13.02 over the repo's pinned 12.0 ceiling (`crap4dart.yaml:35` — "pushes may only make the codebase BETTER, never worse"). I reproduced the gate locally: `crap4dart check --baseline` passes (duplication baselines clean), the failure is exclusively the coverage-driven CRAP ratchet, so it will stay red until the function is restructured.

Fix — keep the mirror complete but flatten the switch. Two shapes that both fit the file's existing patterns (note `config_service.dart` deliberately cannot import `cli_config.dart` — dart:io — so reuse the mirror-by-value style, not the boot parser's private helpers):

